data: {"id":"202609250440483908aa988814432d","created":1790282448,"object":"chat.completion.chunk","model":"glm-5.3-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_1fa9b4f81b024941b56b9a8d","index":0,"type":"function","function":{"name":"Write","arguments":"{\"content\":\"# Cutover and Rollback Plan\\n\\nMigration: user-api database migration (PostgreSQL 14.5 → 16.1)\\n\\nThis document describes the cutover procedure for moving traffic from the old\\ndata store to the new one, and the rollback plan for returning to a safe state\\nif the cutover fails.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Preconditions\\n\\nBefore starting cutover, confirm all of the following:\\n\\n- [ ] `baseline.json` exists and matches the current pre-migration state.\\n- [ ] Shadow comparison (`shadow_compare.py old_state.json new_state.json`)\\n      has been reviewed and all differences are expected.\\n- [ ] `lag_drift.txt` shows small replication lag and `drift_detected: false`.\\n- [ ] A fresh data snapshot/backup of the old store has been taken.\\n- [ ] `dual_rw.log` shows dual read/write traffic is stable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Cutover Steps\\n\\n1. **Freeze writes**\\n   Run the freeze script to stop new writes and mark the migration frozen:\\n\\n   ```bash\\n   ./freeze.sh\\n   ```\\n\\n   This creates `frozen.flag` and prints `Writes frozen`. Verify the flag:\\n\\n   ```bash\\n   test -f frozen.flag && echo \\\"frozen\\\"\\n   ```\\n\\n2. **Drain in-flight work**\\n   Wait for queues and in-flight requests to complete. Confirm no traffic is\\n   still writing to the old store.\\n\\n3. **Verify replication has caught up**\\n   Check lag and drift one final time:\\n\\n   ```bash\\n   cat lag_drift.txt\\n   ```\\n\\n   Proceed only if lag is near zero and `drift_detected` is `false`.\\n\\n4. **Final shadow comparison**\\n   Compare old and new store state snapshots:\\n\\n   ```bash\\n   python3 shadow_compare.py old_state.json new_state.json\\n   ```\\n\\n   Review any differences before continuing.\\n\\n5. **Promote the new store**\\n   Switch the primary role to the new store and update connection\\n   configuration/credentials for the application.\\n\\n6. **Resume writes (dual-write off, single-writes to new store)**\\n   Point all writes at the new store. Reads may remain dual for a short\\n   verification window.\\n\\n7. **Smoke test**\\n   Run application health checks and a sample of read/write operations\\n   against the new store.\\n\\n8. **Record completion**\\n   Update `baseline.json` (or a successor file) with the new engine, version,\\n   schema, and a fresh `data_snapshot` entry.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Rollback Plan\\n\\nTrigger rollback if any of the following occur after promotion: write errors\\non the new store, data drift detection, unacceptable latency, or failed smoke\\ntests.\\n\\n1. **Re-freeze writes**\\n   Run `./freeze.sh` again (remove `frozen.flag` only when ready to unfreeze).\\n\\n2. **Demote the new store**\\n   Revert the primary role: point the application's write path back at the\\n   old store using the previous connection configuration.\\n\\n3. **Restore from snapshot if data was corrupted**\\n   If writes on the new store caused damage, restore the old store from the\\n   pre-migration snapshot referenced in `baseline.json`\\n   (`data_snapshot.location`).\\n\\n4. **Resume writes on the old store**\\n   Remove the freeze flag only after confirming the old store is healthy:\\n\\n   ```bash\\n   rm -f frozen.flag\\n   ```\\n\\n5. **Re-enable dual read/write**\\n   Resume `dual_rw.sh` operation and monitor `dual_rw.log` until a new\\n   cutover attempt is scheduled.\\n\\n6. **Post-mortem**\\n   Record the failure cause and update this document before retrying.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Residue Check\\n\\nAfter a cutover attempt (successful or rolled back), verify no unexpected\\nfiles were left behind by listing files modified in the last 10 minutes:\\n\\n```bash\\nfind . -type f -mmin -10 -not -path './.git/*'\\n```\\n\\nExpected residue after a clean cutover:\\n\\n- `dual_rw.log` (if dual read/write ran)\\n- `frozen.flag` (only if writes are still frozen)\\n- state/snapshot JSON files explicitly updated during cutover\\n\\nAny other recently modified files should be investigated before unfreezing\\nwrites.\\n\",\"file_path\":\"/home/agent/workspace/migration/cutover_rollback.md\"}"}}]}}]}

